course: dictionary
lesson: 8338
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Context means the words and sentences around a word. «We watched a romantic film about two people who met on a train.» Here romantic means about love between people.
explain: The same word can describe a place or a feeling. «The old castle looked romantic in the moonlight.» Nobody is in love here. Romantic means beautiful and dreamy, in a way that stirs the feelings. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: A romantic can also be an idea that is lovely but not realistic. «Her plan to sail round the world on a raft was romantic, but it could never work.» Then romantic can be a noun too: «Mia is a romantic who dreams of love and adventure.» Here a romantic is a person.
explain: A capital R, as in Romantic, is a special word for art and poetry. In an art or history lesson, Romantic means the Romantic movement, when poets and painters loved nature. Check the subject you are studying to find the right meaning.
fact: Romantic can mean about love between people, as in a romantic dinner.
fact: «A couple» means two people in a romantic relationship.
fact: Grown-ups call very sweet romantic film scenes «soppy», and children are allowed to look away or roll their eyes.
fact: Romantic with a capital R means the Romantic movement in art and poetry, when Romantic poets loved nature.
fact: Phrases to know: hopeless romantic, romantic comedy.
exercise: «We watched a romantic film about two people who met on a train.» What does romantic mean here? | Shouting and fast | Very old and grey | *About love between people
exercise: «Mia is a romantic who dreams of love and adventure.» What is a romantic in this sentence? | A kind of cloud | *A person who dreams of love or adventure | A ship's captain
exercise: Grown-ups call very sweet romantic film scenes what word? | treacherous | curt | barely | *soppy
test: «The old castle looked so romantic in the moonlight.» What does romantic suggest? | *Beautiful and dreamy, stirring the feelings | Full of loud noise | Covered in mud
test: «Her plan to sail round the world on a raft was romantic, but it could never work.» What does romantic mean here? | Quite expensive | *Lovely but not realistic | Very dangerous
exam: In an art lesson, what does Romantic with a capital R mean? | Sweet and tasty | *About the Romantic movement in art and poetry | A type of dinner | Very loving between two people
